Third-party models used by voice-local-cli
===========================================

This repository's own code is licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE). The speech
models listed below are downloaded automatically at runtime -- they are never bundled
into this repository or its releases -- and are NOT covered by the MIT License. Each
keeps its own upstream license.

This list needs re-verification against the live model cards before any public release:
model licenses on Hugging Face (pyannote.audio's gated terms in particular) have shifted
across versions before, and this list is not a guarantee that upstream terms haven't
changed since it was last checked.

1. Whisper large-v3-turbo (CPU path)
-------------------------------------
- Used by: dictate.py, transcribe_live.py, transcribe.py (CPU/faster-whisper backend)
- Source: OpenAI, distributed via the `faster-whisper` CTranslate2 conversion
- License: MIT

2. OpenVINO/whisper-large-v3-turbo-int8-ov (Intel GPU path)
-------------------------------------------------------------
- Used by: _openvino_backend.py, when an Intel GPU is available
- Source: https://huggingface.co/OpenVINO/whisper-large-v3-turbo-int8-ov -- a
  pre-converted, quantized build of the same upstream Whisper large-v3-turbo model
- License: MIT (same as the upstream model it's converted from) -- NEEDS
  RE-VERIFICATION against the live model card before publishing

3. jonatasgrosman/wav2vec2-large-xlsr-53-german / -english
--------------------------------------------------------------
- Used by: _align_backend.py, for Call mode's word-level timestamps (forced alignment)
- License: Apache-2.0
- Deliberately NOT using torchaudio's built-in MMS_FA bundle or the ctc-forced-aligner
  package's default model: both rely on the same Meta MMS checkpoint under CC-BY-NC 4.0,
  which restricts commercial use. This project avoids that family entirely instead of
  tracking which specific checkpoint is in play.

4. pyannote/speaker-diarization-3.1
--------------------------------------
- Used by: transcribe.py, for Call mode's speaker diarization
- Source: https://huggingface.co/pyannote/speaker-diarization-3.1 (gated -- requires
  accepting the model's terms on Hugging Face and a personal access token)
- License: not stated here -- check the live model card before publishing; pyannote's
  gated terms have changed across releases before.

Reporting a problem
--------------------
If you believe any model listed above is mischaracterized, or its upstream license has
changed in a way that affects this project's use, open an issue.
